someone to review your proposal  technical support from our team and a  community of like-minded students that  you can interact with and potentially  design even group projects together with  them  so on the portal you will be able to  utilize our system to guide you through  all of the steps that are typically  included in preparing a poster  presentation and here i have a brief  recording of how this is possible to do  on the portal itself so the first step  would be to complete your profile  then you would have to add your bio and  uh connect to your uh orc id or your  social media  and after you do that you will have to  earn 10 000 points by practicing  different types of analyses that we  describe in programs and courses  and complete a course  that speaks about the way that you can  utilize bioinformatics to do a research  project  now after that you can start your own  project  and the project will have several  different sections including an overview  kind of reproducible projects include a  reference data set that is curated and  prepared  so we will go through the process of  submitting that data set on dataverse  and explaining the metadata  we will then talk about all the standard  sections like abstract introduction  methods results discussion and  conclusion including a list of  references and acknowledgments at the  end  now as a result of completing such a  project you will be able to add that  project to your resume or present it at  a poster conference  and so here we have several examples of  people that have submitted either as a  preprint  others have published in the  undergraduate  journals  and others have even used some of the  results that they were working on in  their ongoing research studies  some just use that example to  train  and acquire skills as well  but what's important is that at the end  of the summer  in august we will have our virtual omix  research symposium  this symposium is a bi-annual event that  we organize together 